The adapter's constructor should accept the adaptee as an argument.  Member functions of the adapter will then call corresponding functions of the adaptee, potentially transforming or adapting the results as necessary.  Consider using `using` declarations for concise member function definitions if the adaptee interface closely matches the desired adapter interface.

Example:
`class DequeStackAdapter { 
  std::deque<T> data; 
public:
  DequeStackAdapter() = default; 
  explicit DequeStackAdapter(const std::deque<T>& d) : data(d) {} 
  // ...adapter member functions using data...
};`
